<article class="env-definition" id="0EHY">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0EHY">Definition <span data-tag="0EHY">51.13.1</span>.</a> Let $I$ be an ideal of a Noetherian ring $A$. Let $K \in D^+_{\textit{Coh}}(A)$. We define the <em>$I$-depth</em> of $K$, denoted $\text{depth}_ I(K)$, to be the maximal $m \in \mathbf{Z} \cup \{ \infty \} $ such that $H^ i_ I(K) = 0$ for all $i < m$. If $A$ is local with maximal ideal $\mathfrak m$ then we call $\text{depth}_\mathfrak m(K)$ simply the <em>depth</em> of $K$. </p>
</article>